---
import "../styles/global.css";
import { buildPilotInquiry, PILOT_EMAIL, PILOT_WORKFLOWS } from "../lib/pilot";

const canonicalUrl = new URL("/pilot/", Astro.site ?? Astro.url);
const inquiry = buildPilotInquiry();
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Planning to let an agent issue refunds? Scope a Velvet pilot for one workflow: test the limits, inspect the evidence, and leave with a control plan your team can rerun." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f0e8" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Velvet" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Put your agent’s refund limits to the test — Velvet" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="One workflow. An observed baseline. A control plan your team can rerun. Talk through a Velvet design-partner pilot." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://shadowpath.coriolislabs.ca/og.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <title>Agent refund pilot — Velvet</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="nav-shell">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Velvet home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">V/R</span><span>Velvet</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/protected-refunds/">Inspect the refund evidence ↗</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main" class="section-shell pilot-page">
      <section class="pilot-intro" aria-labelledby="pilot-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">For teams building agents that can issue refunds</p>
        <h1 id="pilot-title">Put your agent’s<br /><span>refund limits to the test.</span></h1>
        <p class="pilot-lede">Before widening your agent’s authority, find out which paths can exceed
          an approval or shared budget. Start with one workflow in an isolated environment and
          leave with evidence your engineering team can act on.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#contact">Discuss your workflow</a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="/protected-refunds/">See the reference evidence</a>
        </div>
        <p class="intro-note">Design-partner pilot · Local and self-hosted · One agreed outcome</p>
      </section>

      <section class="deliverables" aria-labelledby="deliverables-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">What your team takes away</p>
          <h2 id="deliverables-title">A decision you can support with evidence.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverable-grid">
          <article><span>01 / MAP</span><h3>Your refund authority, made explicit.</h3><p>Document the approved amounts, budget and reachable routes: tools, APIs, admin screens, queues and direct writes.</p></article>
          <article><span>02 / TEST</span><h3>A baseline you can inspect.</h3><p>Run isolated trials and independently observe the resulting state. Keep the route inventory, report and evidence together.</p></article>
          <article><span>03 / RETEST</span><h3>A control plan you can rerun.</h3><p>Prioritize the paths that escaped, identify where enforcement belongs, and retain a test command for the next change.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="contact-layout">
        <section class="fit-copy" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">Start small</p>
          <h2 id="fit-title">Bring one workflow.<br />We’ll scope the test together.</h2>
          <p>This is a fit for support automation, AI platform and engineering teams that have a refund workflow and a system owner who can help test it.</p>
          <ol class="scoping-steps">
            <li><strong>First, a scoping conversation.</strong><p>Describe what your agent can do and the limit you need to hold. No integration is needed for this conversation.</p></li>
            <li><strong>Then, an agreed pilot.</strong><p>Choose one outcome, an engineering owner and an isolated test environment or representative fixture. Agree scope, timeline and any fee before work begins.</p></li>
            <li><strong>Finally, an evidence review.</strong><p>Review the observed baseline, unresolved paths and remediation priorities. Your team keeps the project and rerun instructions.</p></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="fit-note"><strong>Working on a different action?</strong><p>Payments, account changes and data exports can be scoped too. Describe your workflow so we can assess fit.</p></div>
        </section>

        <section id="contact" class="contact-card" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">Talk directly with Paul</p>
          <h2 id="contact-title">What should your agent be allowed to do?</h2>
          <p>Send a short note to <a href={`mailto:${PILOT_EMAIL}`}>{PILOT_EMAIL}</a>. These optional details help us start with your workflow.</p>

          <div id="inquiry-fields" hidden>
            <label for="pilot-company">Team or company <span>(optional)</span></label>
            <input id="pilot-company" type="text" autocomplete="organization" maxlength="100" placeholder="Your team" />
            <label for="pilot-workflow">Workflow</label>
            <select id="pilot-workflow">{PILOT_WORKFLOWS.map(workflow => <option>{workflow}</option>)}</select>
            <label for="pilot-details">What limit do you need to hold? <span>(optional)</span></label>
            <textarea id="pilot-details" rows="4" maxlength="600" aria-describedby="inquiry-privacy" placeholder="For example: our support agent can refund orders, but retries and concurrent requests must stay within an approved daily budget."></textarea>
          </div>

          <p id="inquiry-privacy" class="contact-note">Keep this high level. Leave out credentials, customer records and sensitive payment details.</p>
          <div class="contact-actions">
            <a id="pilot-email" class="button button-primary" href={inquiry.mailto}>Open email draft</a>
            <button id="copy-inquiry" class="button button-quiet" type="button" hidden>Copy inquiry</button>
          </div>
          <p class="contact-note">You send the email yourself. This page does not submit or store your inquiry.</p>
          <p id="inquiry-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
          <details id="inquiry-preview" hidden>
            <summary>Preview your inquiry</summary>
            <label for="inquiry-draft" class="draft-label">Email draft</label>
            <textarea id="inquiry-draft" rows="12" readonly>{inquiry.copyText}</textarea>
          </details>
          <noscript><p class="contact-note">The email link works without JavaScript. Add your workflow details in your email app, or write directly to {PILOT_EMAIL}.</p></noscript>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="pilot-boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">What the evidence can establish</p>
        <h2 id="boundary-title">A bounded assessment of your declared paths.</h2>
        <p>Velvet is currently local and self-hosted. Results depend on the routes you inventory,
          the controls deployed and the independent observer. The published refund reference uses a
          single PostgreSQL ledger with synthetic orders; it does not establish guarantees for an
          external payment provider or your deployment.</p>
        <div class="boundary-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/paulchum/velvet-rope/blob/main/docs/public/pilot.md">Full pilot scope ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/paulchum/velvet-rope/blob/main/docs/public/CLAIMS.md">Claim boundaries ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/paulchum/velvet-rope/blob/main/docs/public/shadowpath-quickstart.md">Try it yourself ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="pilot-footer section-shell"><a href="/">← Back to Velvet</a><span>Open source · Apache-2.0</span></footer>
    <script>import "../scripts/pilot";</script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .pilot-page { padding-top: 72px; }
  .pilot-intro { max-width: 940px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
  h1 { margin: 24px 0; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6.2vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 540; letter-spacing: -.06em; line-height: 1.04; }
  h1 span { color: var(--purple); }
  .pilot-lede { max-width: 730px; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .intro-note { margin-top: 20px; font-size: .8rem; }
  .deliverables { padding: 56px 0 72px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  h2, .section-heading h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); letter-spacing: -.04em; line-height: 1.15; }
  h2 { margin: 16px 0 22px; }
  .deliverable-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 32px; }
  article { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 28px; background: var(--surface); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  article > span { font: 700 .7rem monospace; color: var(--purple); }
  article h3 { margin: 28px 0 16px; font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  article p, .fit-copy p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .95rem; }
  .contact-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; align-items: start; gap: 72px; padding: 32px 0 72px; }
  .scoping-steps { padding-left: 22px; margin: 32px 0; }
  .scoping-steps li { padding-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .scoping-steps li::marker { color: var(--purple); font-weight: 750; }
  .scoping-steps p { margin-top: 8px; }
  .fit-note { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 24px; }
  .fit-note p { margin-top: 8px; }
  .contact-card { padding: 32px; border: 1px solid #b797ef; border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-small); scroll-margin-top: 100px; min-width: 0; }
  .contact-card h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .contact-card > p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .contact-card a:not(.button), .boundary-links a { color: var(--purple-deep); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  label { display: block; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 22px 0 8px; }
  label span { font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
  input, select, textarea { width: 100%; min-width: 0; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--white); font: inherit; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  textarea { resize: vertical; }
  input:focus-visible, select:focus-visible, textarea:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--purple); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .contact-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin: 22px 0 14px; }
  .contact-actions .button { flex: 1; cursor: pointer; }
  .contact-card .contact-note { margin-top: 14px; font-size: .78rem !important; }
  #inquiry-status:not(:empty) { margin-top: 16px; padding: 12px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--purple-soft); font-size: .85rem; color: var(--purple-deep); }
  #inquiry-preview { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 16px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .draft-label { margin-top: 16px; }
  #inquiry-draft { font-size: .8rem; }
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .pilot-boundary { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 48px 0 64px; }
  .pilot-boundary p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 840px; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .boundary-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; margin-top: 24px; font-size: .85rem; }
  .pilot-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 28px 0 40px; font-size: .8rem; }
  .nav-shell > a:last-child { font-size: .85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .contact-layout { gap: 36px; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .pilot-page { padding-top: 44px; }
    .pilot-intro { padding-bottom: 48px; }
    .deliverable-grid, .contact-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .deliverables { padding: 40px 0; }
    .contact-layout { padding-bottom: 48px; }
    .contact-card { padding: 24px; }
    .contact-actions { flex-direction: column; }
    .nav-shell { gap: 18px; }
    .nav-shell > a:last-child { max-width: 160px; text-align: right; }
    .pilot-footer { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  }
</style>
